From: Akisaira <akisaira@outlook.com>
Subject: [PATCH] Input: himax-spi: return a failed register write as an error

himax_mcu_register_write() logs a failed data write, then switches the
burst mode as it does after every write and returns what that returned,
normally 0, so every caller takes the failed write as done: power-on
init goes on as if the IC had taken its settings, and the IC command
mailbox hands over a slot whose packet never arrived and moves on to the
next one.  Every caller already checks the return value.  Still switch
the burst mode as after a successful write, and then return the write's
error.

Assisted-by: Claude:claude-opus-5-5
Origin: local
Upstream-Status: Pending
---
 drivers/input/touchscreen/himax-spi-core.c | 9 +++++----
 1 file changed, 5 insertions(+), 4 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/input/touchscreen/himax-spi-core.c b/drivers/input/touchscreen/himax-spi-core.c
index 1f3f76fe06..e7b2922cd9 100644
--- a/drivers/input/touchscreen/himax-spi-core.c
+++ b/drivers/input/touchscreen/himax-spi-core.c
@@ -346,7 +346,7 @@ static int himax_mcu_register_read(struct himax_ts_data *ts, u32 addr, u8 *buf,
 /* Write the internal (SRAM)address and data to AHB register */
 static int himax_mcu_register_write(struct himax_ts_data *ts, u32 addr, const u8 *buf, u32 len)
 {
-	int ret;
+	int ret, burst;
 
 	union himax_dword_data target_addr;
 
@@ -357,11 +357,12 @@ static int himax_mcu_register_write(struct himax_ts_data *ts, u32 addr, const u8
 	target_addr.dword = cpu_to_le32(addr);
 	ret = himax_write(ts, HIMAX_AHB_ADDR_BYTE_0,
 				target_addr.byte, buf, len + HIMAX_REG_SZ);
-	if (ret < 0) {
+	if (ret < 0)
 		dev_err(ts->dev, "%s: write ahb_addr_byte_0 failed\n", __func__);
-	}
 
-	return himax_mcu_set_burst_mode(ts, !(len > HIMAX_REG_SZ));
+	/* switch the burst mode as after a successful write, then report the write's error */
+	burst = himax_mcu_set_burst_mode(ts, !(len > HIMAX_REG_SZ));
+	return ret < 0 ? ret : burst;
 }
 
